Re-assert the attach APN before the attach APN's own context

Stock re-sends SET_INITIAL_ATTACH_APN, byte for byte unchanged, before the
first SETUP_DATA_CALL it makes on a stack. Captured on both stacks of one
Android boot on this firmware (B-16035863):

  f5 Telus:  ATTACH 2896ms -> (PS up 6491ms) -> ATTACH 9932ms  -> ims   11238ms  GRANT
  f6 Fizz:   ATTACH 2820ms -> (PS up 5974ms) -> ATTACH 10358ms -> data  10387ms  GRANT
                                                               -> ims   11332ms  GRANT

We sent the attach once at radio-on and never again. The attach request is what
populates the CP's per-context tables, so re-assert it, once per attach epoch.

Scoped to the context that *is* the attach APN's own, which is the only shape
the capture supports. The wider form -- re-assert before whichever context came
first -- was built, shipped as r38 and measured, and it is wrong: it put the
attach 9 ms ahead of an IMS context for a foreign APN, something stock never
does, and the CP answered 2250 after 19 s where the byte-identical request
without it had been granted in 288 ms.

    r36 f6:  SET_DATA_PROFILE ims -> SETUP cid17 ims            -> GRANT  288ms
    r38 f6:  SET_INITIAL_ATTACH_APN -> SET_DATA_PROFILE ims
                                  -> SETUP cid17 ims            -> 2250  19565ms

Those two AP->CP sequences are identical but for the inserted frame. Two boots
granted that context with no re-assert; the one boot that re-asserted was
refused, and within that same boot the later context -- past the epoch, so
without one -- was granted. Stock's re-assert on the data stack is followed
29 ms later by the attach APN's own context, and that is what this reproduces.

No radio cycle goes with it: stock's only SET_RADIO_POWER on either stack was
at radio-on, and a cycle here would tear down the registration being waited on.
Once per epoch and not once per context, because that is also what stock does --
on f6 its second context followed the first with no attach in between.

